First, calculate the value of one full piggy bank. It holds 100 pennies, which equals $1.00 (since 100 pennies = $1). It also holds 50 dimes, which equals $5.00 (since 50 dimes × $0.10 = $5.00). So, one bank contains $1.00 + $5.00 = $6.00.

Next, since Ivan has filled two piggy banks, multiply the value of one bank by 2: $6.00 × 2 = $12.00.

